   "text": "The run ended with a budget exception and reward 0 after 87 episodes. That is well below the roughly 120-call request budget, so it is classed as a token ceiling. The model spent most of its turns on exploration and an unsuccessful search for upstream code, then made broken edits.\n\nUpstream search:\n- It downloaded docformatter 1.7.7 [T0B22:<RANGE>Saved /tmp/df/docformatter-1.7.7-py3-none-any.whl</RANGE>] and 1.7.8, and grepped for the feature with no hits [T0B42].\n- It tried curling GitHub, which failed [T0B72:<RANGE>rc=7</RANGE>].\n- It concluded \"No internet. So I must implement from scratch.\" [T0B73:<RANGE>No internet. So I must implement from scratch.</RANGE>]\n\nEdits:\n- The structured-region helper concatenates the result of `do_find_directives` with lists. That function returns a bool [T0B150:<RANGE>def do_find_directives(text: str) -> bool:</RANGE>], yet the new code does \"for _idx in _directive_idx + _literal_idx + _doctest_idx + _list_idx + _field_idx:\" [T0B151:<RANGE>for _idx in _directive_idx + _literal_idx + _doctest_idx + _list_idx + _field_idx:</RANGE>]. Adding a bool to a list cannot work at runtime.\n- The first wiring attempt into format.py failed with \"AssertionError\" [T0B170:<RANGE>AssertionError</RANGE>].\n- The second wiring attempt failed with \"IndexError: list index out of range\" [T0B172:<RANGE>IndexError: list index out of range</RANGE>].\n- The transcript shows the feature never wired in and never tested.\n\nNo outside code was used for the edits; they were typed in place.",
